(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "cloud-itonami's legal Service operator changes from Gftd Japan 株式会社 to AWAI Network, L.L.C." "cloud-itonami-partners repo scaffold path — the free-path/self-registration/managed-tier flagship cohort in cloud-itonami itself")), (:adr/topic "cloud-itonami-awai-network-operator-change"), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607232200-cloud-murakumo-dynamics-loop-integration-session-wrapup" "gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo-gap/docs/adr-operator-dynamics-loop-integration.md" "gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo-gap/docs/adr-operator-etzhayyim-mobile-mcc.md" "adr-2607172600-cloud-itonami-isic-5820-salesforce-replace-flagship" "adr-2607161620")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607242100-cloud-itonami-awai-network-operator-change"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-24"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607242100: cloud-itonami Service operator changes to AWAI Network, L.L.C.\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-24\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner instruction, agent-executed)\n**Scope**: `orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami` (child-repo commit `70554ca10d12`, merged to `main` via GitHub API server-side merge), `manifest/west.yml` pin advance (`ad1531f9640c`→`70554ca10d12`, `--entry cloud-itonami`, server-side pin-verified)\n\n## Context\n\ncloud-murakumo's operator was previously changed from Gftd Japan 株式会社 to\n**AWAI Network, L.L.C.** (a Delaware LLC, file number 10704996, formed\n2026-07-20) for reasons specific to that product: cloud-murakumo is designed\nas a decentralized inference-credits/protocol economy (`kotoba-lang/engi`\nconsensus, `kotoba-lang/en` mutual-credit currency, native MCC ledger), and\nkeeping protocol/token governance authority separate from Gftd Japan's B2B\ninfrastructure role was an explicit design decision\n(`gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo-gap/docs/adr-operator-etzhayyim-mobile-mcc.md`,\n`adr-operator-dynamics-loop-integration.md`, superproject\nADR-2607232200). cloud-itonami, by contrast, is a conventional B2B SaaS\n(Japan-governed ToS, JPY Stripe billing, APPI-oriented Privacy Policy) with\nno protocol/token layer — the two products' operators were kept distinct for\nthat reason.\n\nOwner instruction (2026-07-24): unify cloud-itonami under the same Delaware\nLLC already operating cloud-murakumo, rather than maintain Gftd Japan 株式会社\nas cloud-itonami's separate legal operator. This ADR records that change and\nits real, unresolved consequences — it does not re-litigate or reverse the\noriginal rationale for why the two products' operators were set up\nseparately; the owner's instruction supersedes that rationale for\ncloud-itonami specifically.\n\n**Important asymmetry from the cloud-murakumo precedent**: when AWAI Network\nwas named cloud-murakumo's operator, cloud-murakumo had zero real paid\ntransactions. cloud-itonami, at the time of this change, already has a live\ncommercial surface — 4 self-registered external tenants, live Stripe Payment\nLinks across the flagship cohort (6399/6310/7810/5820/851/852/853/854, see\n`90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn`), and the\n`hyp/itonami-smb-pay` gate open (externalPaid still 0). This is an operator\nchange on an already-operating commercial service, not a pre-launch\ndesign decision, and creates real gaps a pre-launch change would not.\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. `orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami` operator identity updated (child-repo commit `70554ca10d12`)\n\n- `legal/terms.md` Section 15 (Contact) and `legal/privacy.md` Section 11\n  (Contact) now name **AWAI Network, L.L.C.** (Delaware file number\n  10704996) as the Service operator / data controller, with Gftd Japan\n  株式会社 named explicitly as infrastructure/software supplier, not the\n  operator. Both sections carry a **[CONFIRM]** marker flagging the\n  Companies Act (Japan) Art. 817/818 foreign-company-registration question\n  and the APPI Art. 24 cross-border-disclosure question respectively (see\n  Decision 3).\n- `src/cloud_itonami/site/footer.cljc` (the shared operator-identity footer\n  rendered on every static route) updated: `operator-name` → \"AWAI Network,\n  L.L.C.\", `operator-corporate-number`/`operator-address` (Gftd Japan's\n  Japan corporate-number/registered-address, no longer the operator's own)\n  replaced with `operator-delaware-file-number` (10704996) and an explicit\n  `operator-infra-note` (\"Infrastructure and software supplied by Gftd Japan\n  株式会社\"). A new footer nav link points to `/legal/company.md`.\n- Regenerated the non-hand-enriched static routes through the existing JVM\n  generator (`clojure -M:local:site`, which deliberately excludes\n  `write-public-cockpit!`/`write-isco-1212!`/`write-isic-6492!` per that\n  generator's own documented hand-enrichment-drift warning): `public/trust/`,\n  `public/partners/`, `public/legal/terms/`, `public/legal/privacy/`.\n  `public/index.html`, `public/isco-1212/index.html` and\n  `public/isic-6492/index.html` carry pre-existing hand-applied enrichment\n  the generator's own source does not reproduce byte-for-byte (documented in\n  `cloud-itonami.site.generate`'s own ns docstring, discovered during\n  ADR-2607185000 Addendum 2) — those three were hand-patched with an exact,\n  minimal textual substitution of only the footer-identity block, verified\n  by diff to touch nothing else.\n- `test/cloud_itonami/site/{trust,partners,legal}_test.cljc` extended to\n  assert `\"AWAI Network\"` is present (in addition to the pre-existing\n  `\"Gftd Japan\"` assertion, which still holds true via the infra-supplier\n  note and continues to pass unchanged). Full `clojure -M:test` run: 1077\n  tests / 7649 assertions; the only failures/errors are pre-existing,\n  network-dependent (`kotoba-xrpc-*`, `doctor-*`) or sandbox-environment\n  (`bb`-binary-dependent) failures unrelated to this change, confirmed by\n  their namespace (none in `cloud-itonami.site.{trust,partners,legal}-test`).\n- New `legal/company.md` (also copied verbatim to `public/legal/company.md`,\n  served as a static file, mirroring cloud-murakumo's own\n  `public/legal/company.md` convention) — an Operator Record modeled\n  directly on cloud-murakumo's, stating the Delaware entity/registered-agent\n  facts and, critically, an honest **\"Known gaps\"** section (Decision 3).\n\n### 2. `manifest/west.yml` pin advanced (superproject, this ADR's own commit)\n\n`--entry cloud-itonami` minimal single-entry diff (1 line): revision\n`ad1531f9640cfc1d476e86151921f39c1d02b60b` → `70554ca10d124af310919f19adca2e3f43a40a62`, `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry cloud-itonami` — server-side pin-verified (fast-forward from old pin, reachable from `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami`'s default branch) before being written.\n\n### 3. Known gaps — recorded honestly, not resolved by this ADR\n\nThis operator change was executed as a documentation/identity change only.\nThe following real, unresolved gaps are documented in\n`orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami/legal/company.md` and are **not** closed by\nthis ADR:\n\n- **Stripe merchant of record.** The live Stripe account processing\n  itonami's Payment Links remains registered under Gftd Japan 株式会社\n  (`docs/deployment-secrets.md`, `src/cloud_itonami/edge/billing.cljc` —\n  neither file was changed by this ADR, since the underlying Stripe account\n  genuinely has not moved). Do not represent AWAI Network as the Stripe\n  merchant of record to a prospective paying customer until the account is\n  re-papered or a documented agency arrangement exists.\n- **Foreign-company registration in Japan.** cloud-itonami's ToS specifies\n  Japan governing law/Tokyo District Court jurisdiction and bills JPY to\n  Japan-resident SMB customers; whether a Delaware LLC operator with no\n  Japan registration triggers Companies Act (Japan) Art. 817/818\n  foreign-company registration has not been reviewed by counsel.\n- **Consumption tax / invoice-system registration** for a foreign operator\n  selling JPY services to Japan customers — not assessed.\n- **APPI Art. 24 cross-border-disclosure** implications of the controller\n  now being organized outside Japan — not reviewed by counsel.\n\n### 4. Explicitly out of scope (owner confirmation, same session)\n\n**itad.gftd.ai** (Gftd Japan's own regulatory license-tracking application)\nand the **gftd.ai** site remain Gftd Japan 株式会社's own operations,\nunrelated to cloud-itonami's operator identity, and are unaffected by this\nchange. `src/cloud_itonami/license.cljc` (Gftd Japan's ITAD license-tracking\nnamespace) was deliberately left untouched.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) cloud-itonami and cloud-murakumo now share one legal operator (AWAI\n  Network, L.L.C.), matching the owner's stated intent to unify the two\n  under the same Delaware LLC.\n- (+) The real gaps this creates are documented honestly and\n  specifically (not glossed over) in `legal/company.md`, following the same\n  disclosure discipline cloud-murakumo's own operator record already\n  established (\"Items requiring counsel/owner completion\").\n- (-) Until the Stripe merchant-of-record gap is closed, there is a live\n  inconsistency between the stated contracting party (AWAI Network) and the\n  entity actually processing customer payment (Gftd Japan's Stripe account)\n  for any of the flagship cohort's Payment Links. This is a real,\n  outstanding item, not merely a template placeholder.\n- (-) The Companies Act / consumption-tax / APPI cross-border questions are\n  genuinely unresolved legal questions for an operating, revenue-seeking\n  Japan-facing service — this ADR does not and cannot resolve them; it\n  flags them for counsel review, per the owner's own chosen path (rewrite\n  documents now, track the mismatch as a known TODO) rather than delaying\n  the operator-identity change until those questions are resolved.\n- No change to cloud-itonami's actual runtime/governor/store code, Stripe\n  account, or ITAD license applications — this ADR is scoped to the\n  Service-operator identity stated in cloud-itonami's own legal/marketing\n  surface, matching the scope the owner selected.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Option | Verdict | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| Keep Gftd Japan 株式会社 as cloud-itonami's operator (status quo) | ❌ | Explicit owner instruction to unify under AWAI Network |\n| Form a second, cloud-itonami-specific Delaware LLC rather than reusing AWAI Network | ❌ | Owner's stated intent was unification under the SAME entity already operating cloud-murakumo, not a third legal entity |\n| Hold the documentation change until the Stripe account and Japan foreign-company-registration basis are actually resolved | ❌ (deferred) | Owner explicitly chose \"rewrite the documents now, track the mismatch as a known TODO\" over waiting; the real-world Stripe/registration work is out of this agent's authority (external legal/financial re-papering) and is follow-up |\n| Treat this as ADR-only (no repo/footer/test changes this session) | ❌ | Owner's decision was to actually execute the document rewrite, not merely record an intent to do so later |\n| Change `src/cloud_itonami/license.cljc` / ITAD references to AWAI Network | ❌ | Owner explicitly confirmed itad.gftd.ai and gftd.ai remain Gftd Japan's own operations, unrelated to this change |\n\n## References\n\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo/public/legal/company.md` (the Operator\n  Record pattern this ADR's `legal/company.md` follows)\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo-gap/docs/adr-operator-dynamics-loop-integration.md`,\n  `adr-operator-etzhayyim-mobile-mcc.md` (AWAI Network's original scope and\n  governance rationale, specific to cloud-murakumo)\n- `90-docs/adr/2607232200-cloud-murakumo-dynamics-loop-integration-session-wrapup.edn`\n- `90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn` (the flagship\n  cohort + live-Stripe-Payment-Link context this ADR's Decision 3 gaps\n  apply to)\n- `orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami` commit `70554ca10d124af310919f19adca2e3f43a40a62`\n  (merged `agent/awai-network-operator` → `main`)\n\n\n## 改訂履歴\n\n（2026-07-25 に `90-docs/adr-ledger/adr-ledger.edn` から統合。以後この文書は最新状態のみを表し、履歴は git が持つ。）

### 2026-07-24 — note

Sharpened the operator-change gaps with cited research (child commit 7f56df7b): foreign-company registration under Companies Act Art. 818 is likely required for an ongoing Japan-targeted subscription business (not merely open) and is now the highest-priority item, with a PE tax-exposure caveat; consumption tax likely does NOT require JCT registration given cloud-itonami is B2B-only (Japan's reverse-charge mechanism applies instead), and a customer reverse-charge notice was added to legal/terms.md Section 6.3; the prior pass's APPI citation was wrong (Article 24, cross-border transfer OUT of Japan) and is corrected to Article 171 (extraterritorial application), a narrower/simpler finding. Also added legal/payment-collection-agency-agreement.md, an unsigned DRAFT documenting Gftd Japan's Stripe account collecting on AWAI Network's behalf -- makes the Stripe merchant-of-record mismatch a concrete, reviewable document without claiming it resolves anything until executed. None of this is legal advice; every item still needs counsel review. manifest/west.yml pin advanced --entry cloud-itonami (7f56df7becd6, server-side verified).
"), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/date "2026-07-24"), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607242100: cloud-itonami Service operator changes to AWAI Network, L.L.C."), (:adr/source-format "edn")))
